{%- comment -%}
  main-product — the product page. One section, branching on product type.

  Built 31/08/2026. Third pass: live's buy-box pattern from sections/
  product-block.liquid, which is the section behind live's engagement rings.
  Plain wedding rings first; other types branch off `is_plain`.

  NOT PORTED AS MARKUP. Live runs TWO product pages — product-block (56KB) for
  configurable diamond rings, main-product (162KB, T4S) for plain rings. Both
  are too big to read whole and neither is worth copying. This merges the two
  behaviours into one section, per Ed's call, built from the data and from
  live's rendered pages.

  ── THE DATA MODEL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  A plain wedding ring is ONE PRODUCT PER metal + profile + width + weight.
  Its variants are RING SIZES ONLY: 70 of them, A to Z+9.5, each priced a
  little above the last because a bigger ring uses more metal.

    options              Ring Size (the only one)
    custom.ring_metal    "14ct Yellow Gold"
    custom.ring_profile  "Concave"
    custom.ring_weight   "Heavy Weight"
    custom.spin_360      a Sirv .spin URL
    filters.band_width   "2mm"

  Two consequences that shape this whole file:

  1. SIZE IS A VARIANT, so the page states a RANGE at the top and a SELECTED
     price by the button. Two different questions, two different numbers.
  2. METAL IS NAVIGATION. Choosing platinum means going to another product.

  NO OVERSIZE SURCHARGE ON PLAIN RINGS. Ed, 31/08/2026: the 10%-above-size-Q
  surcharge that product-block applies does NOT apply here, because the metal
  cost is already in the variant ladder — applying both would charge twice. It
  DOES apply to every other ring type, where size is a line-item property with
  no price of its own. When those branches are built they set the
  `_size_surcharge` property that the Oversize Ring Surcharge cart-transform
  function reads. Do not add it to this branch.

  ── THE METAL SWITCHER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Two axes, as live's engagement page does it: COLOUR as round swatches, CARAT
  as a separate row. Ten flat squares said less and read as noise.

  Handles are perfectly systematic, verified 31/08/2026:

      {metal}-{profile}-wedding-ring-{width}-{weight}
      14ct-yellow-gold-concave-wedding-ring-2mm-heavy
      platinum-concave-wedding-ring-25mm-medium

  so each target is CONSTRUCTED and looked up with all_products. No app, no
  metafield list, no JS.

    · `all_products` is capped at TWENTY unique handles per page. Five colours
      plus three carats is eight. Adding profile or width switchers the same
      way would blow through it — they need a different mechanism. The side-
      diamond panel spends four more; that is the current total.
    · a handle that does not exist renders that option disabled rather than as
      a dead link. Platinum and palladium have no carat, so the carat row
      simply does not apply to them.
    · the width slug is irregular: 2.5mm appears in handles as "25mm", so it
      comes from `filters.band_width | remove: '.'`, not from `handle`, which
      would give "2-5mm" and 404.

  ── ENGRAVING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  £55, interior, on every ring type. Copied from product-block, mechanism and
  all: a Yes/No toggle revealing a 35-character input, a counter and a font
  select. The text and font ride along as line-item properties; the MONEY is a
  separate cart line for a hidden fee product, added by fye-ui.js. Shopify
  cannot post two line items from one product form, which is why that add is
  AJAX rather than a plain submit.

  The fee variant id is a SETTING, not a constant — a hardcoded variant id in
  markup is a silent failure the day someone recreates the fee product.

  ── THE STONE CHOOSERS — added 31/08/2026 evening ─────────────────────────

  Two OPTIONAL PANELS rendered after the buy box, not a third branch. Most
  engagement rings get neither. Ed, 31/08/2026.

    fye-buybox-centre   semi-mounts: all three of fye.centre_shape,
                        carat_min, carat_max, plus enable_centre_diamond
    fye-buybox-sides    trilogies: tag "Trilogy Ring" + fye.side_stones.code,
                        plus enable_side_diamonds

  THE THREE CHOICES ARE INDEPENDENT AND NONE OVERLAPS. Ed, 31/08/2026 — worth
  stating because live's code implies otherwise and it cost a wrong turn:

    · "Diamond Quality" is the SHOULDER diamond quality. It always was. With
      Metal it forms the variant, so it sets the variant price.
    · the centre diamond is its own cart line, at its own price.
    · the side pair is its own cart line, at its own price.

  So a trilogy with diamond-set shoulders offers all three and nothing is
  charged twice. Live hides the quality row on any trilogy carrying a
  side_stones metafield (its W333) and locks the ring to its cheapest natural
  grade; that behaviour is DELIBERATELY NOT PORTED, because it takes away a
  real choice. Live's other rule — hiding the row on PLAIN-shouldered rings,
  where the grade buys nothing — is a fair refinement and is still outstanding;
  it is about plain shoulders, not about trilogies.

  NOTHING IS SELECTED BY DEFAULT in either panel. Ed, 31/08/2026. Live
  preselects the dearest route, which lets a shopper reach the basket without
  ever making the decision. The cost of that choice is a REQUIREMENT on
  fye-ui.js: add to cart must be blocked until each rendered panel has a mode,
  because an unselected chooser is an incomplete order, not a neutral one.

  Neither panel present = the page exactly as it was before they existed.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign p = product
  assign cf = p.metafields.custom
  assign fye = p.metafields.fye

  assign ring_type = cf.ring_type.value | first | default: p.type
  assign is_plain = false
  if ring_type contains 'Plain Wedding'
    assign is_plain = true
  endif

  assign current = p.selected_or_first_available_variant

  comment
    Sibling handles: the parts that stay fixed while metal changes.
  endcomment
  assign profile_slug = cf.ring_profile | handle
  assign width_slug = p.metafields.filters.band_width | remove: '.'
  assign weight_slug = cf.ring_weight | split: ' ' | first | downcase
  assign can_switch = false
  if is_plain and profile_slug != blank and width_slug != blank and weight_slug != blank
    assign can_switch = true
  endif

  comment
    Split the metal into its two axes. "14ct Yellow Gold" -> 14ct + Yellow
    Gold. "Platinum" -> no carat, colour is the whole string.
  endcomment
  assign metal_now = cf.ring_metal
  assign carat_now = ''
  assign colour_now = metal_now
  if metal_now contains 'ct '
    assign carat_now = metal_now | split: ' ' | first
    assign colour_now = metal_now | remove_first: carat_now | strip
  endif
  assign carat_digits = carat_now | remove: 'ct'
  if carat_digits == blank
    assign carat_digits = '18'
  endif

  assign colours = 'Yellow Gold,White Gold,Rose Gold,Platinum' | split: ','
  assign carats = '18ct,14ct,9ct' | split: ','
  assign golds = 'Yellow Gold,White Gold,Rose Gold' | split: ','

  comment
    ── Chooser gates ──
    All three metafields for the centre panel, per Ed 31/08/2026. The -SMT SKU
    tail is not the gate, though 30 of 30 sampled -smt products satisfy both.

    Blank comparisons on possibly-nil metafields are safe here. Liquid parses
    `a and b` RIGHT TO LEFT, so a condition whose right-hand side can throw
    (nil.size, a number compared with nil) has to be nested instead — see
    live's product-block for what that looks like when it goes wrong.
  endcomment
  assign show_centre = false
  if s.enable_centre_diamond and fye.centre_shape != blank and fye.carat_min != blank and fye.carat_max != blank
    assign show_centre = true
  endif

  assign show_sides = false
  if s.enable_side_diamonds and p.tags contains 'Trilogy Ring' and fye.side_stones.value.code != blank
    assign show_sides = true
  endif
-%}

<section class="band band--white pdp" data-screen-label="Product">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pdp__top">

      {%- comment -%} ---- Gallery ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdp__gallery" data-fye-gallery>
        <div class="pdp__stage">
          {%- if p.media.size > 0 -%}
            {%- for media in p.media limit: 8 -%}
              <div class="pdp__panel{% if forloop.first %} is-on{% endif %}" data-fye-panel="{{ forloop.index0 }}">
                {{ media | image_url: width: 1400 | image_tag:
                   loading: forloop.first | default: false | replace: true, 'eager' | default: 'lazy',
                   widths: '400,600,900,1200,1400',
                   sizes: '(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 55vw',
                   alt: media.alt | default: p.title,
                   class: 'pdp__img' }}
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="pdp__panel is-on pdp__panel--empty"></div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            The 360. A panel like any other; its Sirv viewer is inert until
            fye-ui.js loads the script, which it does the first time this panel
            is opened. Nothing is requested on a page nobody rotates.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if cf.spin_360 != blank -%}
            <div class="pdp__panel pdp__panel--spin" data-fye-panel="spin">
              <div class="Sirv pdp__spin"
                   data-fye-spin
                   data-src="{{ cf.spin_360 }}"
                   data-options="autospin: off; hint.text: Drag to rotate; hint.type: drag;"></div>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if p.media.size > 1 or cf.spin_360 != blank -%}
          <ul class="pdp__thumbs">
            {%- for media in p.media limit: 8 -%}
              <li>
                <button class="pdp__thumb{% if forloop.first %} is-on{% endif %}"
                        type="button"
                        data-fye-thumb="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                        aria-label="View image {{ forloop.index }}">
                  {{ media | image_url: width: 220 | image_tag:
                     loading: 'lazy',
                     widths: '110,220',
                     sizes: '96px',
                     alt: '' }}
                </button>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}

            {%- if cf.spin_360 != blank -%}
              <li>
                <button class="pdp__thumb pdp__thumb--spin"
                        type="button"
                        data-fye-thumb="spin"
                        aria-label="View in 360 degrees">
                  {{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 220 | image_tag:
                     loading: 'lazy',
                     widths: '110,220',
                     sizes: '96px',
                     alt: '' }}
                  <span class="pdp__spinbadge" aria-hidden="true">360°</span>
                </button>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ---- Buy box ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdp__buy">

        <h1 class="pdp__title">{{ p.title }}</h1>

        <p class="pdp__range">
          {%- if p.price_varies -%}
            Price range {{ p.price_min | money }} – {{ p.price_max | money }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ p.price | money }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>

        <div class="pdp__meta">
          {%- if current.sku != blank -%}
            <p class="pdp__metarow"><span class="pdp__metakey">SKU</span> <span data-fye-sku>{{ current.sku }}</span></p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if p.collections.size > 0 -%}
            {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
            <p class="pdp__metarow">
              <span class="pdp__metakey">Categories</span>
              {%- for c in p.collections -%}
                {%- unless c.handle == 'all' -%}
                  {%- if shown > 0 -%}<span aria-hidden="true">, </span>{%- endif -%}
                  <a href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.title }}</a>
                  {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
                {%- endunless -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if p.description != blank -%}
          <div class="pdp__desc rte">{{ p.description }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---- Metal: colour, then carat ---- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if can_switch -%}
          <div class="pdp__field">
            <p class="pdp__label pdp__label--inline">Metal: <span class="pdp__labelval">{{ metal_now }}</span></p>

            <ul class="pdp__colours">
              {%- for colour in colours -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign is_gold = false
                  if golds contains colour
                    assign is_gold = true
                  endif

                  if is_gold
                    assign target_metal = carat_digits | append: 'ct ' | append: colour
                  else
                    assign target_metal = colour
                  endif

                  assign sib_handle = target_metal | handle | append: '-' | append: profile_slug | append: '-wedding-ring-' | append: width_slug | append: '-' | append: weight_slug
                  assign sib = all_products[sib_handle]

                  assign is_current = false
                  if colour == colour_now
                    assign is_current = true
                  endif

                  if is_gold
                    assign tone = colour | split: ' ' | first | downcase | prepend: '-' | prepend: carat_digits | prepend: '--metal-'
                  elsif colour == 'Platinum'
                    assign tone = '--metal-platinum'
                  else
                    assign tone = '--platinum'
                  endif
                -%}
                <li>
                  {%- if is_current -%}
                    <span class="pdp__colour is-current" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});" aria-current="true">
                      <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
                      <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ colour }}</span>
                    </span>
                  {%- elsif sib != blank -%}
                    <a class="pdp__colour" href="{{ sib.url }}" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});">
                      <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
                      <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ colour }}</span>
                    </a>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <span class="pdp__colour is-off" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});">
                      <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
                      <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ colour }}</span>
                      <span class="visually-hidden">not made in this profile and width</span>
                    </span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>

            {%- comment -%}
              Carat only applies to the golds. Platinum and palladium have no
              carat, so the row is absent rather than disabled — an empty row
              of greyed buttons would imply we might make a 9ct platinum.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if golds contains colour_now -%}
              <ul class="pdp__carats">
                {%- for carat in carats -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign target_metal = carat | append: ' ' | append: colour_now
                    assign sib_handle = target_metal | handle | append: '-' | append: profile_slug | append: '-wedding-ring-' | append: width_slug | append: '-' | append: weight_slug
                    assign sib = all_products[sib_handle]
                    assign is_current = false
                    if carat == carat_now
                      assign is_current = true
                    endif
                  -%}
                  <li>
                    {%- if is_current -%}
                      <span class="pdp__carat is-current" aria-current="true">{{ carat | upcase }}</span>
                    {%- elsif sib != blank -%}
                      <a class="pdp__carat" href="{{ sib.url }}">{{ carat | upcase }}</a>
                    {%- else -%}
                      <span class="pdp__carat is-off">{{ carat | upcase }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- form 'product', p, class: 'pdp__form', id: 'pdp-form' -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current.id }}" data-fye-variant-id>

          <script type="application/json" data-fye-variants>
            [
              {%- for v in p.variants -%}
                {"id":{{ v.id }},"title":{{ v.title | json }},"price":{{ v.price | json }},"sku":{{ v.sku | json }},"available":{{ v.available }}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            ]
          </script>

          {%- if is_plain -%}
          {%- if p.has_only_default_variant == false -%}
            {%- for option in p.options_with_values -%}
              <div class="pdp__field">
                <label class="pdp__label" for="pdp-opt-{{ forloop.index }}">
                  {{ option.name }}
                  {%- if option.name == 'Ring Size' and s.size_guide_url != blank -%}
                    <a class="pdp__sizelink" href="{{ s.size_guide_url }}">Find my size</a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </label>
                <select class="pdp__select" id="pdp-opt-{{ forloop.index }}" name="options[{{ option.name | escape }}]" data-fye-option>
                  {%- for value in option.values -%}
                    <option value="{{ value | escape }}"{% if option.selected_value == value %} selected{% endif %}>{{ value }}</option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- render 'fye-buybox-eternity', product: p, settings: s, current: current -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              The choosers. AFTER the ordinary buy box, because the metal and
              shoulder-quality choices come first in the customer's head: what
              the ring is made of, then what goes in it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if show_centre -%}
              {%- render 'fye-buybox-centre', product: p, settings: s -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if show_sides -%}
              {%- render 'fye-buybox-sides', product: p, settings: s -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if s.engraving and s.engraving_variant_id != blank -%}
            <div class="pdp__engrave"
                 data-fye-engrave
                 data-fee-variant="{{ s.engraving_variant_id }}"
                 data-fee-price="{{ s.engraving_price_pennies | default: 5500 }}">
              <div class="pdp__engravehead">
                <p class="pdp__label">
                  {{ s.engraving_label | default: 'Custom engraving' }}
                  <span class="pdp__labelval">{{ s.engraving_price_label | default: '+£55' }}</span>
                </p>
                <div class="pdp__seg" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ s.engraving_label | default: 'Custom engraving' | escape }}">
                  <button type="button" role="radio" data-fye-engrave-set="no" class="is-on" aria-checked="true">No</button>
                  <button type="button" role="radio" data-fye-engrave-set="yes" aria-checked="false">Yes</button>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="pdp__engravebody" data-fye-engrave-body hidden>
                <div class="pdp__engraverow">
                  <input class="pdp__input"
                         type="text"
                         name="properties[Engraving]"
                         data-fye-engrave-text
                         maxlength="{{ s.engraving_max | default: 35 }}"
                         placeholder="{{ s.engraving_placeholder | default: 'Engraving' | escape }}"
                         disabled>
                  <span class="pdp__count" data-fye-engrave-count>0/{{ s.engraving_max | default: 35 }}</span>
                </div>

                {%- if s.engraving_fonts != blank -%}
                  <select class="pdp__select" name="properties[Engraving font]" data-fye-engrave-font disabled>
                    <option value="">Select a font</option>
                    {%- assign font_list = s.engraving_fonts | split: '|' -%}
                    {%- for f in font_list -%}
                      <option>{{ f | strip }}</option>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </select>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          <p class="pdp__selected">
            <span class="pdp__selectedkey">Selected price</span>
            <span class="pdp__selectedval" data-fye-price>{{ current.price | money }}</span>
          </p>

          <button class="btn btn--block pdp__atc" type="submit" name="add" data-fye-atc{% unless current.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
            {%- if current.available -%}
              {{ s.atc_label | default: 'Add to bag' }}
            {%- else -%}
              {{ s.mto_label | default: 'Made to order — enquire' }}
            {%- endif -%}
          </button>
        {%- endform -%}

        {%- if s.enquire_label != blank -%}
          <a class="btn btn--outline btn--block" href="{{ s.enquire_link | default: '/pages/contact-us' }}">{{ s.enquire_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- render 'fye-wishlist-button', product: p -%}

        {%- if s.reassurance != blank -%}
          <p class="pdp__reassure fine">{{ s.reassurance }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.fye .pdp__top {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--s10);
  align-items: start;
}

/* --- gallery ------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__stage {
  position: relative;
  background: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .pdp__panel {
  display: none;
}

.fye .pdp__panel.is-on {
  display: block;
}

.fye .pdp__img {
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  object-fit: cover;
}

.fye .pdp__panel--empty {
  aspect-ratio: 1;
}

.fye .pdp__spin {
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  width: 100%;
  background: var(--white);
}

.fye .pdp__thumbs {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--s2);
  margin: var(--s2) 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.fye .pdp__thumbs > li {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__thumb {
  position: relative;
  display: block;
  width: 96px;
  padding: 0;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  background: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .pdp__thumb:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .pdp__thumb.is-on {
  border-color: var(--line-strong);
}

/* The 360 badge sits over its thumbnail rather than beside it, so the row
   stays one rhythm of squares. */
.fye .pdp__spinbadge {
  position: absolute;
  inset-block-end: var(--s1);
  inset-inline-end: var(--s1);
  padding: 2px 6px;
  background: var(--white);
  color: var(--teal);
  font-size: 10px;
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
}

/* --- buy box ------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__buy {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s5);
}

.fye .pdp__title {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-h3);
}

.fye .pdp__range {
  margin: calc(var(--s5) * -1 + var(--s2)) 0 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s2);
  padding-bottom: var(--s5);
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__metarow {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
}

.fye .pdp__metakey {
  display: inline-block;
  min-width: 88px;
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__desc {
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
}

.fye .pdp__field[hidden] {
  display: none;
}

.fye .pdp__field {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s3);
}

.fye .pdp__label {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__label--inline { justify-content: flex-start; gap: var(--s2); }

.fye .pdp__labelval,
.fye .pdp__labelnote,
.fye .pdp__sizelink {
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  letter-spacing: 0;
  text-transform: none;
}

.fye .pdp__labelval {
  color: var(--ink);
}

.fye .pdp__sizelink {
  border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
}

/* --- metal: colour dots, then carat --------------------------------------
   Round, per Ed. The only curves in the brand are the logo flourish and the
   monogram — and now these, because a metal swatch is a picture of a ring's
   colour, not a UI surface. Named beneath, because five golds are hard to
   tell apart at 44px and impossible for anyone colour-blind. */

.fye .pdp__colours {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--s5);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.fye .pdp__colours > li {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__colour {
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s2);
  width: 92px;
  text-align: center;
}

.fye .pdp__dot {
  display: block;
  width: 44px;
  height: 44px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--sw);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--gem-edge);
}

.fye .pdp__colour.is-current .pdp__dot {
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--gem-edge), 0 0 0 2px var(--white), 0 0 0 3px var(--teal);
}

.fye .pdp__colour:hover .pdp__dot {
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--gem-edge), 0 0 0 2px var(--white), 0 0 0 3px var(--sage);
}

.fye .pdp__colourname {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__colour.is-current .pdp__colourname {
  color: var(--ink);
}

.fye .pdp__colour.is-off {
  opacity: 0.35;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

.fye .pdp__carats {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--s2);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.fye .pdp__carats > li {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__carat {
  background: none;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-width: 80px;
  min-height: 44px;
  padding-inline: var(--s4);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-button);
}

.fye .pdp__carat:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .pdp__carat.is-current {
  background: var(--teal);
  border-color: var(--teal);
  color: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .pdp__carat.is-off {
  opacity: 0.35;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

/* --- form ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__form {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s5);
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__select,
.fye .pdp__input {
  width: 100%;
}

/* --- engraving ----------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .pdp__engrave {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s3);
  padding-top: var(--s5);
  border-top: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__engravehead {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
}

.fye .pdp__seg {
  display: flex;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
}

.fye .pdp__seg button {
  min-width: 72px;
  min-height: 44px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  background: transparent;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-button);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink);
}

.fye .pdp__seg button + button {
  border-inline-start: 0;
}

.fye .pdp__seg button.is-on {
  background: var(--teal);
  border-color: var(--teal);
  color: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .pdp__engravebody[hidden] { display: none; }

.fye .pdp__engravebody {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s3);
}

.fye .pdp__engraverow {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s3);
}

.fye .pdp__count {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

/* --- stone choosers -----------------------------------------------------
   Centre diamond and side diamonds. Both snippets share this vocabulary;
   it stays here rather than in core because only this section renders them
   (conventions §2 — core earns an addition at two sections, not one). */

.fye .pdp__choose {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s3);
  padding-top: var(--s5);
  border-top: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__choosenote {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* Three mode cards ACROSS, per Ed 31/08/2026. Each is its own bordered tile
   with its own edge, rather than one divided stack — three tiles read as
   three options at a glance, which a stack with dividers does not.

   Equal columns rather than auto-fit: the three are peers and a widow column
   would imply one matters more. The copy in each card is kept to a few words
   for the same reason — at ~200px a sentence wraps to four lines. */
.fye .pdp__modes {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--s2);
  margin-top: var(--s2);
}

.fye .pdp__mode {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s1);
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: var(--s3) var(--s4) var(--s4);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  background: var(--white);
  text-align: start;
  transition: background var(--dur) var(--ease), border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

.fye .pdp__mode:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

/* Chosen: a changed ground and a darker edge — Ed, 31/08/2026. No radio dot
   and no heavy left rule; the tile itself carries the state. Ivory rather
   than a teal fill so both levels of type keep their contrast (ink on ivory
   is 8.2:1, ink-soft 5.5:1 — a teal fill would drop the second line below
   AA). --line-strong resolves to teal, so the edge is unmistakable. */
.fye .pdp__mode.is-on {
  background: var(--ivory);
  border-color: var(--line-strong);
}

.fye .pdp__modetitle {
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  color: var(--ink);
}

.fye .pdp__modecopy {
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* Pinned to the foot of the tile so the three fees line up across the row
   however long each explanation runs. */
.fye .pdp__modefee {
  margin-block-start: auto;
  padding-block-start: var(--s2);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  color: var(--ink);
}

.fye .pdp__modebody[hidden] { display: none; }

/* Mist is the design system's info-panel ground and is what live uses here.
   It also does the structural job: the body is visibly the consequence of the
   tile above it rather than another section of the page. */
.fye .pdp__modebody {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s3);
  padding: var(--s4);
  background: var(--mist);
}

/* ink-soft on mist measures 4.5:1 — exactly at the AA limit (see fye-core).
   The panel's own explanatory copy carries the full level instead, and soft
   is left for genuinely secondary lines. */
.fye .pdp__modebody .pdp__choosenote {
  color: var(--ink);
}

.fye .pdp__stonestate {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__stonebtn {
  align-self: flex-start;
}

/* The chosen stone, once picked. */
.fye .pdp__stone[hidden] { display: none; }

.fye .pdp__stone {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr auto;
  gap: var(--s3);
  align-items: center;
  padding: var(--s3);
  background: var(--white);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
}

.fye .pdp__stoneimg {
  width: 64px;
  height: 64px;
  object-fit: cover;
  background: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .pdp__stonename {
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
}

.fye .pdp__stonesub {
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__stoneprice {
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
}

/* Chips: side-diamond grades, and the picker's colour / clarity filters. */
.fye .pdp__chips {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--s2);
}

.fye .pdp__chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 2px;
  min-height: 44px;
  min-width: 44px;
  padding: var(--s2) var(--s3);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  background: var(--white);
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: var(--ink);
  transition: background var(--dur) var(--ease), border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

.fye .pdp__chip:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

/* Same logic as the mode tiles: ground plus a darker edge, not a teal fill,
   because the chip carries a price line under its name. */
.fye .pdp__chip.is-on {
  background: var(--ivory);
  border-color: var(--line-strong);
}

.fye .pdp__chipname {
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
}

.fye .pdp__chipprice {
  font-size: 11px;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__waiver {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
  gap: var(--s3);
  align-items: start;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: var(--ink);
  text-transform: none;
  letter-spacing: 0;
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* --- the picker modal ---------------------------------------------------
   One set of markup at every width (conventions §3): the stone grid drops to
   one column and the filter block is a real <details> on a phone. */

.fye .pdp__modal[hidden] { display: none; }

.fye .pdp__modal {
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 60;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  padding: var(--s5);
}

.fye .pdp__modalscrim {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background: var(--scrim);
}

.fye .pdp__modalpanel {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 1080px;
  max-height: 88vh;
  background: var(--white);
  border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
}

.fye .pdp__modalhead {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
  padding: var(--s5);
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__modaltitle {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-h4);
}

.fye .pdp__modalsub {
  margin: var(--s2) 0 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__modalx {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  width: 44px;
  height: 44px;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--teal);
}

.fye .pdp__modalx:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
  color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .pdp__filters {
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__filterssum {
  display: none;
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: var(--s3) var(--s5);
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.fye .pdp__filtersbody {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(190px, 1fr));
  gap: var(--s4) var(--s5);
  padding: var(--s5);
}

.fye .pdp__filter {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s2);
}

.fye .pdp__filterlbl {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__filterval {
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  letter-spacing: 0;
  text-transform: none;
  color: var(--ink);
}

/* Two range inputs stacked in one track: a dual-range without a library.
   Both sit in the same grid cell; JS keeps min <= max. */
.fye .pdp__range {
  display: grid;
}

.fye .pdp__range input {
  grid-area: 1 / 1;
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 0;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: transparent;
}

.fye .pdp__modaltools {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
  padding: var(--s3) var(--s5);
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .pdp__count {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__toolsright {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s3);
}

.fye .pdp__sortlbl {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__sort {
  width: auto;
  min-height: 44px;
}

/* The results are the only scrolling part, so the head, filters and footer
   stay put while a long list moves. */
.fye .pdp__stones {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  overflow-y: auto;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr));
  gap: var(--s4);
  padding: var(--s5);
}

.fye .pdp__stonecard {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s2);
  padding: 0;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  background: var(--white);
  text-align: start;
}

.fye .pdp__stonecard:hover {
  border-color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .pdp__stonecard.is-on {
  border-color: var(--line-strong);
  background: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .pdp__stonecardmedia {
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  background: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .pdp__stonecardmedia img,
.fye .pdp__stonecardmedia video {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
}

.fye .pdp__stonecardbody {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 2px;
  padding: var(--s3);
}

.fye .pdp__stoneflag {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__stoneempty {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
  padding: var(--s7) 0;
  text-align: center;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .pdp__modalfoot {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: flex-end;
  gap: var(--s4);
  padding: var(--s5);
  border-top: var(--hairline);
}

/* --- breakpoints. Media queries LAST, always. ---------------------------- */

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .fye .pdp__top {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s7);
  }
}

@media (max-width: 749px) {
  /* The filter block becomes a real disclosure, closed by default — six
     filter groups above the stones is the whole screen on a phone. */
  .fye .pdp__filterssum {
    display: block;
  }

  .fye .pdp__filters:not([open]) .pdp__filtersbody {
    display: none;
  }

  .fye .pdp__modal {
    padding: 0;
  }

  .fye .pdp__modalpanel {
    max-width: none;
    max-height: 100vh;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
  }

  .fye .pdp__modalhead,
  .fye .pdp__filtersbody,
  .fye .pdp__stones,
  .fye .pdp__modalfoot {
    padding: var(--s4);
  }
}

@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .pdp__colours {
    gap: var(--s4);
  }

  .fye .pdp__colour {
    width: 64px;
  }

  .fye .pdp__engravehead {
    align-items: stretch;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s3);
  }

  .fye .pdp__seg button {
    flex: 1 1 0;
  }

  /* Three tiles across a phone leaves ~100px each, which cannot hold a title
     and a line of explanation. Stacking is the same markup, one column — not
     a second copy (conventions §3). */
  .fye .pdp__modes {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  }

  .fye .pdp__modefee {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .fye .pdp__stones {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(140px, 1fr));
  }

  .fye .pdp__modaltools {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--s2);
  }

  .fye .pdp__modalfoot .btn {
    flex: 1 1 0;
  }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Main product",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "fye-main-product",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Buy box" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "atc_label", "label": "Add to bag label", "default": "Add to bag" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mto_label", "label": "Unavailable label", "default": "Made to order — enquire" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "size_guide_url", "label": "Ring size guide" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "enquire_label", "label": "Secondary button label", "default": "Contact us about this ring" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "enquire_link", "label": "Secondary button link" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "reassurance",
      "label": "Reassurance line",
      "default": "Handmade to order in the UK. Free delivery, complimentary resizing for a year."
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Stone choosers" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Both panels are gated by the product's own data as well as these tickboxes. The centre panel needs all three of fye.centre_shape, carat_min and carat_max; the side panel needs the Trilogy Ring tag and fye.side_stones. Most engagement rings get neither. Nothing is selected by default, so add to cart stays blocked until the shopper chooses."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_centre_diamond", "label": "Offer a centre-diamond choice", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_side_diamonds", "label": "Offer a side-diamond choice", "default": true },

    { "type": "text", "id": "centre_heading", "label": "Centre panel heading", "default": "Centre diamond" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "centre_picker_label", "label": "Picker button label", "default": "Choose your diamond" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "centre_help_link", "label": "\"We will help you choose\" link" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "centre_fee_variant_id",
      "label": "Centre setting fee variant ID",
      "default": "58461224927616"
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "centre_fee_price_pennies",
      "label": "Centre setting fee in pennies",
      "default": 8000
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "centre_supplied_note",
      "label": "Centre \"supply your own\" note",
      "default": "Send us your stone once your order is placed and we will grade, set and finish it with the ring."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "centre_waiver_text",
      "label": "Centre waiver wording",
      "default": "I understand that stones supplied by me are set at my own risk, and that For Your Eternity cannot be held liable for damage to a stone we have not graded."
    },

    { "type": "text", "id": "sides_heading", "label": "Side panel heading", "default": "Side diamonds" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sides_fee_variant_id",
      "label": "Side setting fee variant ID",
      "default": "58739448938880"
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "sides_fee_price_pennies",
      "label": "Side setting fee in pennies"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "sides_waiver_text",
      "label": "Side waiver wording",
      "default": "I understand that stones supplied by me are set at my own risk, and that For Your Eternity cannot be held liable for damage to a stone we have not graded."
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Engraving" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The fee is charged as a separate cart line for a hidden fee product. Without a valid variant ID the whole engraving control is hidden rather than shown and uncharged."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "engraving", "label": "Offer engraving", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "engraving_label", "label": "Label", "default": "Custom engraving" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "engraving_price_label", "label": "Price label", "default": "+£55" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "engraving_variant_id", "label": "Fee variant ID", "default": "58467296018816" },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "engraving_price_pennies",
      "label": "Fee in pennies",
      "default": 5500
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "engraving_placeholder", "label": "Placeholder", "default": "Engraving (35 characters max)" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "engraving_max",
      "label": "Maximum characters",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "ch",
      "default": 35
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "engraving_fonts",
      "label": "Fonts (pipe-separated)",
      "default": "Classic Script|Elegant Serif|Modern Sans|Block Capitals"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Main product" }]
}
{% endschema %}
